Revision history for RabbitMQ::Connection

0.91
    - send() takes optional content_type (default still text/plain) and
      message_id; without them a message is published exactly as before.
    - receive() adds props => { content_type, message_id, delivery_mode },
      holding the properties the publisher set; existing keys are unchanged.
    - Add reject(delivery_tag, channel, requeue) (basic.reject). requeue => 0
      dead-letters through the queue's x-dead-letter-exchange. Refused on a
      publisher-confirm connection, which is publish-only.
    - declare_queue() takes an optional arguments hashref (string values as
      longstr, Perl integers as signed 64-bit). Without it, no arguments are
      sent, as before.

0.9
    - Add publisher confirms with confirm_select().
    - A successful close() resets connection-lifetime state, so a cleanly
      closed object can be reconnected.
    - Confirmed send() reports ack, returned, nack, or timeout.
    - Handle mandatory unroutable publications correctly: basic.return
      followed by basic.ack reports returned.
    - Publisher-confirm connections are publish-only; a timeout or protocol
      failure leaves the settlement state unknown, and the connection must be
      discarded.

0.8
    - Configurable heartbeat.
